 "title": "2cos²x + 3 sin x = 3",
 "caption": "Replacing cos²x by 1 − sin²x gives 2sin²x − 3 sin x + 1 = 0, so sin x = ½ or sin x = 1. On the graph of 2cos²x + 3 sin x the line y = 3 is met at 30°, 90° (where the curve just touches it) and 150°.",
 "alt": "The graph of y = 2cos²x + 3 sin x from 0° to 360° with the line y = 3 touching or crossing it at 30°, 90° and 150°.",
 "description": [
  "Rewrite cos²x = 1 − sin²x: 2sin²x − 3 sin x + 1 = 0.",
  "Factorise: (2 sin x − 1)(sin x − 1) = 0.",
  "sin x = ½ gives 30° and 150°; sin x = 1 gives 90°.",
  "These are the three places the curve reaches the line y = 3."
